	<key>CFBundleVersion</key>
	<string>$(FLUTTER_BUILD_NUMBER)</string>
	<!-- Declared here so App Store Connect stops asking the export-compliance
	     questionnaire on every single upload. Read docs/export-compliance.md
	     before touching this.

	     True, not false: the app ships its own cryptography rather than only
	     calling Apple's. venta_mls links OpenMLS (RFC 9420) for end-to-end
	     message encryption, and WebRTC.framework carries BoringSSL for
	     DTLS-SRTP. Neither is covered by the exemptions, which are for
	     HTTPS/CryptoKit/Keychain, authentication-only use, or DRM. It said
	     false until 2026-08-01, which is why no build was ever asked - that
	     was a false declaration, not a clever trick.

	     No ITSEncryptionExportComplianceCode accompanies it, and that is
	     correct rather than an omission. Apple's reference table
	     (developer.apple.com/help/app-store-connect/reference/
	     export-compliance-documentation-for-encryption) maps our case -
	     "industry standard algorithm, not provided within the Apple operating
	     system" - to exactly one document: the French encryption declaration.
	     Its own footnote limits that to apps "distributing on the App Store in
	     France". CCATS is required only for *proprietary* algorithms; every
	     primitive here is published - HPKE, X25519, Ed25519, AES-GCM,
	     ChaCha20-Poly1305, HKDF - so this is a self-classified ECCN 5D992.c
	     mass market item and CCATS does not apply. No France, no document, no
	     code to match, so a bare true is complete.

	     **This is load-bearing on App Store availability.** A true with no code
	     was tried on 2026-08-01 and altool rejected it:

	       Invalid Export Compliance Code ... key value [] ... (90592)

	     The most likely reason is that availability still included France (the
	     default is every territory), which makes the declaration mandatory and
	     the code with it. So: if France is ever added back under Pricing and
	     Availability, this key stops being sufficient - either file the French
	     declaration and pin the returned code here alongside it, or remove the
	     key entirely and go back to answering the questionnaire per build.
	     Do not "fix" a 90592 by flipping this to false. -->
	<key>ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption</key>
	<true/>
	<key>LSRequiresIPhoneOS</key>
	<true/>
	<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
